## 9. Risk Assessment

| Risk | Impact | Mitigation Strategy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| PHI compliance and HIPAA coverage | Potential legal liability and breach penalties if patient health data is not protected according to regulations. | Select Azure services covered by a Business Associate Agreement (BAA), enable encryption at rest and in transit, enforce strict RBAC, and configure Azure Monitor logs for audit trails. Conduct a compliance audit before go‑live. |
| Budget overruns from Cosmos DB serverless and Azure AD B2C usage | Monthly costs could exceed the $20k ceiling, jeopardizing project financial constraints. | Implement Azure Cost Management alerts, cap RU consumption, regularly review usage patterns, and consider switching to a lower‑cost storage option (e.g., Azure Table Storage) if consumption grows. Use the free tier of Azure AD B2C where possible. |
| Usability for patients with low computer literacy and intermittent connectivity | Low adoption rates may force continued reliance on paper forms, negating efficiency gains. | Design an ultra‑simple, large‑button UI with progressive disclosure, add offline support via Service Workers that cache the questionnaire and sync when online, and provide on‑site tablets/kiosks for assisted completion. |
| Integration gap with existing paper‑based workflow | Without a clear export or printing mechanism, staff may still need manual transcription, increasing workload. | Add a server‑side PDF generation endpoint that produces printable versions of completed questionnaires, and create a simple admin portal for staff to view, export, or print responses. |

